/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1035 0 R
/E (the ultimate expression of Subjective Technology. Turkle explains that objects become evocative when it transcends the bounds of instrumental purpose. They are no longer just tools but thing we think with. objects become emotional objects when they carry powerful personal and symbolic meanings. they might trigger memories, help people process complex emotions, or become a tangible piece of your personal history and identity)
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
